  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"230\"><strong data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"145\">Glucose in body fluids</strong> (e.g., <strong data-start=\"153\" data-end=\"213\">pleural, peritoneal, pericardial, or cerebrospinal fluid</strong>) is measured to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"232\" data-end=\"597\">\n<li data-start=\"232\" data-end=\"321\">\n<p data-start=\"234\" data-end=\"321\">Help distinguish between <strong data-start=\"259\" data-end=\"302\">infectious, inflammatory, and malignant</strong> causes of effusion</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"322\" data-end=\"415\">\n<p data-start=\"324\" data-end=\"415\">Assess <strong data-start=\"331\" data-end=\"367\">glucose transport or consumption</strong> by cells, bacteria, or tumor cells in the fluid</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"416\" data-end=\"500\">\n<p data-start=\"418\" data-end=\"500\">Differentiate <strong data-start=\"432\" data-end=\"471\">transudative vs exudative effusions</strong>, especially in pleural fluid</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"501\" data-end=\"597\">\n<p data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"597\">Support diagnosis in cases of <strong data-start=\"533\" data-end=\"547\">meningitis</strong>, <strong data-start=\"549\" data-end=\"560\">empyema</strong>, <strong data-start=\"562\" data-end=\"578\">tuberculosis</strong>, or <strong data-start=\"583\" data-end=\"597\">malignancy</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"599\" data-end=\"735\">Fluid glucose is typically compared to <strong data-start=\"638\" data-end=\"655\">serum glucose</strong>, with a fluid-to-serum ratio often being more informative than absolute values.</p>\n<p data-start=\"599\" data-end=\"735\">Decreased Levels &ndash; Clinical Implications</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation of Low Fluid Glucose</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Bacterial infections (e.g., empyema, peritonitis)</strong></td>\n<td>Bacteria and neutrophils consume glucose in the fluid</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Tuberculosis</strong></td>\n<td>Glucose is metabolized by immune and TB cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Malignancy</strong></td>\n<td>Tumor cells actively metabolize glucose</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Rheumatoid effusion or lupus pleuritis</strong></td>\n<td>Inflammatory cells consume glucose</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"599\" data-end=\"735\">&nbsp;</p>",
